    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d17">

                <pb facs="0122" n="28" xml:id="pg28"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00 R 296/379: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kellogg</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-06-24T20:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 24, 1924—8
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 24—7:05
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>223. Have just received invitation referred to in my 220, June 18, 4 p.m. It is
                    in form of long memorandum setting forth views of British Government and urging
                    American participation. It is now being coded, and will be sent tomorrow morning
                    at latest.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
